### 2. Update `ui.js` - Add Chat Deduplication in Store

```js client/src/store/ui.js
// ... existing imports and state ...

export const actions = actionTree(
  { state, getters, mutations },
  {
    // ... existing actions ...

    openChat(_, chat) {
      const existingPanel = state._desktopApi?.panels.find(panel =>
        panel.params?.chat?.id === chat.id
      )

      if (existingPanel) {
        existingPanel.api.setActive()
        return
      }

      $storex.ui.showApp({
        name: chat.name,
        component: 'chat',
        params: {
          chat: {
            id: chat.id,
            name: chat.name,
            owner_project_id: chat.owner_project_id
          }
        }
      })
    },

    // ... rest of actions ...
  },
)
```

## Key Changes

1. **`addAppPanel()` method**: Added check for existing chat panels before creating a new one
2. **`findExistingChatPanel()` method**: Searches for a panel with matching chat ID
3. **`activatePanel()` method**: Sets an existing panel as active
4. **`openChat()` action in store**: Added deduplication logic before showing the app

This ensures that clicking on a chat that's already open will activate that tab instead of creating a duplicate.

